@startuml
title Implemented S4 - all nine patterns, atomic commits and post-commit delivery
actor "Application caller / integration test" as Caller
participant BookingFacade as Facade
participant CommittedEventDispatcher as Dispatch
participant AppointmentAssembler as Assembler
participant AppointmentBuilder as Builder
participant AppointmentModeFactory as Mode
participant "AppointmentService decorator chain" as Extras
participant AppointmentCreator as Creator
participant InMemoryAppointmentRepository as Repo
participant ReservationRules as Rules
participant AvailabilityStrategy as Strategy
participant AppointmentEventPublisher as Publisher
participant NotificationListener as Notify
participant AuditListener as Audit
participant ExternalCalendarAdapter as Adapter
participant SimulatedExternalCalendarClient as Legacy
Caller -> Facade : book(commandId, request)
Facade -> Dispatch : execute(commandId, command, operation)
critical dispatcher monitor (shared per repository)
  alt receipt already exists
    Dispatch --> Facade : original BookingResult (different input rejects)
  else new command
    Dispatch -> Assembler : execute facade operation / assemble(request)
    Assembler -> Repo : resolve immutable catalogs
    Assembler -> Builder : id/customer/provider/service/start/mode/extras
    Builder -> Mode : createMeetingDetails + createParticipationInstructions
    Assembler -> Builder : build(injected creator, time)
    Builder -> Extras : quote(service)
    Builder -> Creator : create(validated spec)
    Creator -> Creator : overridden createAppointment(spec)
    Creator --> Assembler : pending appointment subtype
    Assembler --> Dispatch : candidate via facade operation
    Dispatch -> Repo : reserve(candidate, strategy)
    critical repository mutation lock
      Repo -> Repo : capture time, check latest state/catalog/ID
      Repo -> Rules : validate intrinsic and collision constraints
      Rules -> Strategy : preparationBuffer(provider)
      Rules -> Rules : validate effective occupancy/hours
      alt rejected
        Repo --> Dispatch : exception; no mutation or event
      else accepted
        Repo -> Repo : commit reservation + revision + immutable event
        Repo --> Dispatch : committed appointment
      end
    end
    opt successful commit (repository lock released)
      Dispatch -> Repo : events() snapshot in global commit order
      loop each undelivered committed event
        Dispatch -> Publisher : publish(event)
        Publisher -> Notify : onAppointmentEvent(event)
        Notify --> Publisher : success or isolated RuntimeException
        Publisher -> Audit : onAppointmentEvent(event)
        Audit --> Publisher : success or isolated RuntimeException
        Dispatch -> Adapter : synchronize(event)
        Adapter -> Legacy : apply(code, ID, epoch millis, zone, rN, event ID)
        Legacy --> Adapter : success or numeric legacy error
        Adapter --> Dispatch : success or typed warning
      end
      Dispatch -> Dispatch : retain receipt and warnings
      Dispatch --> Facade : BookingResult(snapshot, revision, warnings)
    end
  end
end
Facade --> Caller : result or rejected-command exception
note over Facade, Repo
Confirm/cancel/complete/reschedule operate on latest stored Appointment.
State delegates eligibility and immutable replacement.
Same event/delivery path follows each successful mutation.
External conflicts warn after commit; local repository owns collision prevention.
No callbacks hold the repository mutation lock. Console calls this facade.
end note
@enduml
